  "rules": [
    "Google sign-in, Brand Account, YouTube channel and legal publisher are different objects; no one-to-one count can be assumed.",
    "Studio and the Analytics API serve authorized channel reports, whereas public Data API resource counts cannot expose a competitor's owner earnings.",
    "Advertiser-side Google Ads view/billing events and YouTube public/engaged playback counts have different definitions.",
    "AdSense for YouTube settles conditional earnings, which are different from advertiser invoices and creator profit after costs.",
    "Channel subscribers, people watching, paid service customers and advertisers are overlapping but not interchangeable populations.",
    "An account delegate may operate one or more channels without automatically becoming the payee or sole legal owner.",
